#: titles/common/hunt_opponents.gd:26
msgid "Just learned the game. Plays fast, and loves the tigers."
msgstr "Oyunu yeni öğrendi. Hızlı oynar ve kaplanlara bayılır."

#. Name of a computer opponent in Bagh Chal: Maya, a Nepali woman, with "Didi" ("older sister", a respectful way to address a woman in Nepal). Write it in your script as a name (e.g. ru Майя Диди, ja マヤ・ディディ); languages written in Latin letters keep "Maya Didi".
#: titles/common/hunt_opponents.gd:31
msgid "Maya Didi"
msgstr "Maya Didi"

#. One line about the computer opponent Maya Didi, who runs a tea stall. "When she's looking": she plays well when she isn't distracted.
#: titles/common/hunt_opponents.gd:33
msgid "Plays between customers at her tea stall. Steady, when she's looking."
msgstr "Çay tezgâhında müşterilerin arasında oynar. Dikkati dağılmadıkça istikrarlıdır."

#. Name of a computer opponent in Bagh Chal: Hari, a Nepali man, with "Dai" ("older brother", a friendly way to address a man in Nepal). Write it in your script as a name (e.g. ru Хари Дай, ja ハリ・ダイ); languages written in Latin letters keep "Hari Dai".
